    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ETAMU_External/job/Commerce-TX/Assistant-Professor---Mathematics_R-097884-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor - Mathematics Agency East Texas A&M University Department Mathematics Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help.   Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator.   If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@etamu.edu   A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee.   In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY: The Department of Mathematics at East Texas A&M University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning in Fall 2027. We seek a candidate with expertise in Statistics, Data Science, Machine Learning, or a closely related area. Candidates whose research connects mathematics and statistics with interdisciplinary applications, such as mathematical biology, biostatistics, artificial intelligence, computational science, or related fields, are especially encouraged to apply.   The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, maintain an active research agenda, mentor students, and contribute to the service mission of the department, college, university, and profession. The department is particularly interested in candidates who can support and further develop programs in Statistics and Data Science. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Mathematics, Statistics, and Data Science in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. Contribute to the development and expansion of courses and curricula in Statistics, Data Science, Machine Learning, and related areas. Maintain an active scholarly research program that leads to publications in peer-reviewed scholarly publications, professional presentations, and pursuit of external funding opportunities. Engage undergraduate and graduate students in research and mentorship. Advise and mentor students in academic and professional development. Provide service to the Department, College, University, community, and profession. Maintain effective, professional, and collegial relationships with faculty, students, staff, alumni, and external partners. Maintain on-campus office hours and participate in departmental activities. Serve on departmental, college, and university committees as assigned. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: ·         Education: An earned Ph.D. in Mathematics, Statistics, Data Science, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field (degree must be completed prior to the start date). Experience / Knowledge / Skills: Evidence of potential for excellence in university-level teaching. Demonstrated potential to establish and sustain a productive research program. ·         Ability to: Ability to interact with students, staff, and faculty in a professional, collegial, and collaborative manner. ·         Licensing/Professional Certifications: N/A ·         Physical Requirements: N/A ·         Other Requirements: NA PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: ●        Research expertise in Statistics, Data Science, Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, Computational Mathematics, or related disciplines. ●        Experience teaching Statistics, Data Science, Machine Learning, or related courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. ●        Evidence of interdisciplinary collaboration. ●        Demonstrated record of scholarly publications and professional presentations. ●        Success in obtaining, or strong potential to obtain, external research funding. ●        Commitment to student success, mentoring, and academic excellence. SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: NA APPLICATION MATERIALS: Please submit the following at our Employment website, https://www.etamu.edu/human-resources/employment/ : •      Cover Letter •      Curriculum Vitae •      Statement of Teaching Philosophy •      Statement of Research Interests •      Three professional references with complete contact information (unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered) •      Transcripts (unofficial transcripts will be accepted with the application; official transcripts are required upon verbal offer) All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ETAMU_External/job/Commerce-TX/Assistant-Professor---Psychology---Special-Education_R-097867-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Psychology & Special Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor - Psychology & Special Education Agency East Texas A&M University Department Psychology & Special Ed Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help.   Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator.   If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@etamu.edu   A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee.   In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY:  Are you a clinician-scholar who wants to shape a doctoral program from the ground up? East Texas A&M University is developing a new PsyD in Clinical/School Psychology, and we invite applications for a Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology to help lead the way. The position begins Fall 2027.   As a student-ready Doctoral University classified as R2: High Research Activity by the Carnegie Classification, East Texas A&M offers the resources of a research institution alongside a genuine commitment to student success. The Department of Psychology and Special Education is growing, and this is a rare opportunity to join at a pivotal moment, when your ideas can influence curriculum, training philosophy, and program culture for years to come.   The successful candidate will teach and conduct research in our established Master of Science in Clinical Psychology program, preparing students to deliver evidence-based assessment and intervention. You will also play a central role in developing and delivering the forthcoming PsyD, with opportunities to teach other graduate courses across the department. Alongside teaching, you will build an impactful research program and contribute meaningful service to the department, university, and profession.   To help you launch your research program, we offer private lab space, a dedicated graduate research assistant, and a reduced teaching load during your first year, giving you the time and support to establish your lab and get your scholarship off to a strong start.   We are seeking a dedicated scholar and educator who is excited about graduate training, committed to evidence-based practice, and motivated by the opportunity to build something new. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and sustain a productive research program leading to peer reviewed publications, conference presentations, and other scholarly contributions; Mentor and engage both graduate and undergraduate students in research Provide teaching excellence to graduate students in Clinical Psychology; Teach courses Clinical Psychology, including Psychopathology and Diagnosis, Personality Psychology, Assessment, and others at the graduate level; Prepare syllabi;  Update course materials;  Develop curriculum;  •      Work collaboratively with faculty and staff to implement departmental programs; Provide service to the department, college, university and public schools, and community; and Maintain knowledge and stay abreast of evidence-based assessment and intervention research, and technological applications in the classroom, including online teaching. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: ·         Education: Doctoral degree (Ph.D. or PsyD) in Clinical Psychology (or closely related field) prior to Fall 2027. Experience / Knowledge / Skills: Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work collaboratively with a team of professionals. Good written and oral communication skills. Commitment to high quality teaching. ·         Ability to: Ability to interact with students, staff, and faculty in a professional, collegial, and collaborative manner. ·         Licensing/Professional Certifications: N/A ·         Physical Requirements: N/A ·         Other Requirements: Ability to work beyond normal office hours and/or work on weekends. Ability to travel. PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: ●        Licensed (or license eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Texas. ●        Experience mentoring graduate and/or undergraduate students in research. ●        University teaching experience, including at the graduate level. Online teaching experience. ●        Demonstrated ability to contribute to curriculum development in clinic psychology. SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: NA All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
