      "title": "Open Rank Professor - Management Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nJob Title Open Rank Professor - Management Science Agency East Texas A&M University Department MGT, MKT & MGT SCI Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help.   Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator.   If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@etamu.edu   A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee.   In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY: The College of Business (COB) at East Texas A&M University is seeking a rank-open faculty member in Management Science focused on Supply Chain/Operations. The position is a full-time, 9-month, tenure track position. The successful candidate will teach graduate and undergraduate courses in management science fields with a heavy focus on supply chain areas including operations, efficiency, production, logistics, etc. This position will report to the Department of Management, Marketing, and Management Science and will contribute through teaching, research, and service.   ETAMU is a fast-growing R2 public university with a strong reputation for academic excellence, research innovation, and student success. With over 140+ degree programs, a 20:1 student-to-faculty ratio, and nationally ranked online and graduate programs, ETAMU is committed to transforming lives through quality education. Our employees benefit from a collaborative community, cutting-edge research opportunities, and outstanding resources. This position is not eligible for Visa sponsorship.   DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop, implement, and review effective teaching/learning processes, incorporating appropriate methodology, technology and other tools; Participate in curriculum development and assessment as needed; Remain current in discipline and update course content when appropriate;  Follow university and system polices; Adhere to AACSB accreditation standards and faculty qualifications; Maintain appropriate schedule of office hours; Collaborate with faculty, staff, and external partners to support program development and community engagement; Participate in institutional, college and departmental service roles as assigned; and Other duties as assigned by the Department Head and/or Dean. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Education: A terminal degree in a relevant business field of study from a university with an AACSB accredited business program aligned with Supply Chain Operations Experience / Knowledge / Skills: Earned terminal degree in the field within the past five years and/or peer reviewed journal publications within the last 5 years sufficient to maintain AACSB Scholarly Academic status and supportive of a university with R2 research status Must be able to be qualified as graduate faculty PREFERRED EDUCATION/SKILLS/EXPERIENCE: Holds one or more relevant and active credentials such as Certified Supply Chain Professional, Certified Production & Inventory Management, Certified Logistics, Transportation, & Distribution, ISM Professional in Supply Management, Certified Lean Practitioner, or Lean Six Sigma. Previous teaching experience SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: Supervises faculty and staff in the department All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ETAMU_External/job/Commerce-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice---Counseling_R-097385-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice - Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Practice - Counseling Agency East Texas A&M University Department Counseling Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help.   Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator.   If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@etamu.edu   A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee.   In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY: The Department of Counseling at East Texas A&M University, a student-ready, Doctoral University classified as R2: High Research Activity by the Carnegie Classification—invites applications for a 9-month, full-time, non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Practice (Professional Track Faculty) starting Fall 2027. The successful candidate will serve as the Practicum & Internship Coordinator for the CACREP-accredited programs, with a commensurate instructional workload in recognition of this responsibility.   The chosen candidate will contribute to the department's teaching and service missions. Specifically, we seek a colleague with a demonstrated record of effective teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels; a commitment to meaningful service to the department, college, university, and profession; and an expertise in play therapy or clinical supervision as evidenced by the applicant’s teaching and service contributions. In addition, the candidate must demonstrate professional identity in counseling/counselor education through the following activities: (a) sustained memberships in professional counseling organizations (e.g., ACA, ACES, APT, CSI, TAAP, TCA, etc.); (b) relevant professional counseling credentials (e.g., licensed professional counselor, licensed professional counselor-supervisor, licensed chemical dependency counselor, Registered Play Therapist ™, Registered Play Therapist-Supervisor™, etc.); and (c) sustained professional engagement in professional development and renewal activities, professional service and advocacy in counseling, ongoing counseling practice, and research and scholarly activity in counseling.   DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: TEACHING Teach up to three courses each fall and spring semester across undergraduate and graduate programs Contribute to the department's core curriculum and develop graduate and undergraduate courses in areas of expertise. Deliver instruction online (asynchronously and synchronously) and face-to-face at any university campus (Commerce, Dallas, Plano). Pursue certifications, trainings, and workshops that demonstrate commitment to effective and innovative pedagogy. Stay current on trends and best practices in counseling and one's area(s) of expertise. Advise undergraduate and graduate students. Respond to student inquiries within established university, college, and department expectations, and provide timely, meaningful feedback on assignments, assessments, and evaluations. Foster a supportive learning environment that promotes student persistence, competency attainment, and timely completion of coursework. Perform other duties as assigned. SERVICE & INSTITUTIONAL ENGAGEMENT Participate collegially in departmental, college, and university committees; institutional effectiveness initiatives; accreditation activities; strategic priorities; and other service responsibilities as assigned. Collaborate with faculty and staff to implement departmental initiatives and programs. Participate in required faculty meetings, commencement ceremonies, professional development activities, college events, planning sessions, and other institutional engagement opportunities. Contribute to the professional counseling community through activities such as reviewing, presenting at conferences, and serving in professional organizations. Engage in outreach or community service consistent with the mission of the university. Complete all required university training and assigned administrative responsibilities in a timely manner. Perform other duties as assigned. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Earned doctoral degree in counseling/counselor education; have a related doctoral degree and have been employed as a full-time faculty member in a counselor education program for a minimum of one full academic year before July 1, 2013; have been employed as a full-time doctoral-level faculty member in a CORE-accredited master’s program before July 1, 2017; or have graduated from a rehabilitation doctoral program before January 1, 2018. Academic background (e.g., teaching, research, service) commensurate with the rank of Assistant Professor of Practice. Evidence of scholarly productivity or potential for scholarly productivity in research/creative activity commensurate with rank. Evidence of effective teaching or teaching potential at the university level, including online and in-person graduate-level instruction. Active and sustained memberships in professional counseling organizations. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to travel to any university instruction site (e.g., Commerce, Dallas, Plano). Relevant professional counseling credentials (e.g., licensed professional counselor, licensed professional counselor-supervisor, licensed chemical dependency counselor, certified school counselor, registered play therapist supervisor, registered play therapist, etc.) or licensure/certification eligibility with a commitment to obtain within the first year of their academic appointment. PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: Earned doctoral degree in counseling/counselor education from a CACREP-accredited program. Relevant teaching experience at the graduate level in a CACREP-accredited program, commensurate with the rank of Assistant Professor of Practice. Evidence of training and/or experience teaching counseling coursework online, both synchronously and asynchronously. Knowledge of and familiarity with CACREP standards and the accreditation process. Dissertation committee member experience. Credentialed as a Licensed Professional Counselor-Supervisor (LPC-S). Expertise in play therapy or clinical supervision, with credentialing appropriate to the area of expertise: Play therapy : Member of the Association for Play Therapy and credentialed as a Registered Play Therapist-Supervisor™; or Clinical supervision : Approved Clinical Supervisor (ACS) credential administered by the Center for Credentialing & Education (CCE).   SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: None All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ETAMU_External/job/Commerce-TX/Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor---Director---Counseling_R-097097-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Associate Professor & Director - Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor/Associate Professor & Director - Counseling Agency East Texas A&M University Department Counseling Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help. Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator. If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@etamu.edu A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY: The Department of Counseling at East Texas A&M University - a student-ready, Doctoral University classified as R2: High Research Activity by the Carnegie Classification - invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor or tenured Associate Professor position. The successful candidate will hold the E. Lee Doyle Endowed Professorship title and serve as the Director of East Texas A&M University's Play Therapy & Expressive Arts Center, an Approved Center of Play Therapy Education by the Association for Play Therapy, beginning Fall 2027. The chosen candidate will contribute to the department's teaching, research, and service missions. Specifically, we seek a scholar with a focused research agenda; a demonstrated record of effective teaching at the graduate and/or undergraduate level; a commitment to meaningful service to the department, college, university, and profession; and an expertise in play therapy as evidenced by the candidate’s teaching, research, and service contributions. In addition, the candidate must demonstrate professional identity in counseling/counselor education through the following: (a) sustained memberships in professional counseling organizations (e.g., APT, ACA, ACES, APT, CSI, TAAP, TCA, etc.); (b) relevant professional counseling credentials (i.e., licensed professional counselor-supervisor, Registered Play Therapist-Supervisor™; and (c) sustained professional engagement in professional development and renewal activities, professional service and advocacy in counseling, ongoing counseling practice, and research and scholarly activity in counseling. *Candidates being considered for a tenured appointment at the rank of Associate Professor must be evaluated against, and meet, the department's tenure and promotion criteria as part of the hiring process. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: RESEARCH •  Develop and sustain a productive program of research/creative activity specifically in Play Therapy, leading to peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and other scholarly contributions; •  Engage in efforts to secure external funding for research appropriate to counseling and play therapy; •  Direct and serve on doctoral dissertation committees; and •  Mentor and engage both graduate and undergraduate students in research. TEACHING •  Teach two courses each fall and spring semester across undergraduate and graduate levels; •  Contribute to the department’s core curriculum and develop graduate and undergraduate courses in areas of expertise; •  Deliver instruction both online, asynchronously and synchronously, and face-to-face at any of the university campuses (i.e., Commerce, Dallas, Plano); •  Demonstrate commitment to effective and innovative pedagogy through certifications, trainings, and workshops; •  Maintain knowledge and stay abreast of current trends and best practices in counseling and play therapy; and •  Active advisement of students at the undergraduate and graduate levels. SERVICE Serve as the Director of East Texas A&M University's Play Therapy & Expressive Arts Center Participate collegially in departmental, college, and university committees. Collaborate with faculty and staff to implement departmental initiatives and programs. Contribute to the professional counseling community through activities such as reviewing, presenting at conferences, and serving in professional organizations. Engage in outreach or community service consistent with the mission of the university. DIRECTOR Oversee East Texas A&M University's Play Therapy & Expressive Arts Center, including daily operational management, supervision of graduate assistants and staff, compliance with ethical and licensure/certification standards, and coordination of services, budgeting, and community partnerships. Designing and delivering play therapy coursework and continuing education that meet APT's approved curriculum standards; Supervise play therapy training, practicum, and clinical experiences for students; Maintaining compliance with APT accreditation requirements and renewal processes as an Approved Center and Approved Provider; Organize and advertise approved Play Therapy trainings Mentoring students and supervisees toward Registered Play Therapist™ (RPT™) credentialing; Pursue scholarship and grant funding to support the Center's research and training mission; Cultivate community partnerships to expand clinical training opportunities for students; and Represent the East Texas A&M University's Play Therapy & Expressive Arts Center within the department, university, and broader play therapy community.   MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: An earned doctorate in counseling/counselor education from a CACREP-accredited program; have a related doctoral degree and have been employed as a full-time faculty member in a counselor education program for a minimum of one full academic year before July 1, 2013; have been employed as a full-time doctoral-level faculty member in a CORE-accredited master's program before July 1, 2017; or have graduated from a rehabilitation doctoral program before January 1, 2018; Member of the Association for Play Therapy and licensed as a Licensed Professional Counselor-Supervisor (LPC-S) and credentialed as a Registered Play Therapist-Supervisor™ (RPT-S™); Academic background (i.e., teaching, research, and service) commensurate with the applicant's sought rank, including evidence of, or potential for, scholarly productivity in play therapy research/creative activity, and evidence of, or potential for, effective teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels (online and in-person); Sustained professional engagement, including active memberships in professional counseling organizations, ongoing counseling practice, and professional development/renewal activities; Strong interpersonal and communication skills; Ability to travel to any university instruction site (e.g., Commerce, Dallas, Plano); and Relevant professional counseling credentials (i.e., licensed professional counselor-supervisor and Registered Play Therapist-Supervisor™) or licensure/certification eligibility with a commitment to obtain within the first year of the academic appointment. PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: ·   Relevant teaching experience at the graduate level in a CACREP-accredited program commensurate with rank;   Evidence of training and/or experience teaching counseling coursework online, synchronously and asynchronously;   Previous Clinical Director experience at a counseling center;   Knowledge of and familiarity with CACREP standards and the accreditation process; and  Dissertation committee experience as chair and/or co-chair. SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: NA All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ETAMU_External/job/Commerce-TX/Research---Instruction-Librarian_R-096614-1": {
      "title": "Research & Instruction Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nJob Title Research & Instruction Librarian Agency East Texas A&M University Department Library Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description SUMMARY: The Research and Instruction Librarian is responsible for providing general and advanced discipline-specific research assistance and instruction services to undergraduate and graduate students, faculty, and staff of a designated college, including collection development and engagement, with a focus on coordinating and assessing the multi-literacy program.  As a proud member of the third-largest institution in the Texas A&M University System, ETAMU fosters a strong professional environment that supports career growth and academic excellence. ETAMU is a fast-growing public university with a strong reputation for academic excellence, research innovation, and student success. With over 140+ degree programs, a 20:1 student-to-faculty ratio, and nationally ranked online and graduate programs, ETAMU is committed to transforming lives through quality education. Our employees benefit from a collaborative community, cutting-edge research opportunities, and outstanding resources. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Coordinates and implements an engaging information literacy program and develops student learning outcomes.  Assesses the effectiveness of the literacy program’s strategies and initiatives in support of student success.    Develops and implements policies, procedures, programs, and partnerships to build and improve research skills and integrates information literacy components within courses, curriculum, and the learning management system (LMS).  Creates standards for teaching and learning materials and oversees the creation and maintenance of digital learning objects.  Serves as primary contact for early college high school students. Provides library instruction, develops and creates print and online instructional materials, plans and conducts classes and workshops, and integrates multi-literacies into the teaching, learning, and research activities of the university. Provides research assistance (in-person, phone, chat, email, video conferencing, etc.) and serves as a subject librarian to a designated college/academic department. Collaborates with colleagues and faculty to facilitate collection development to align scholarly resources with the teaching and research needs of the university and college. Plans and participates in engagement activities and events and fosters collaborations with students, faculty, and staff in support of student success and retention.  Participates in the assessment of research and user engagement activities.   Serves on library and university committees. Participates in continuing education and professional development opportunities. Other duties as assigned. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Education: Master's degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA-accredited program. Experience / Knowledge / Skills: Excellent oral and written communication skills and interpersonal skills. Attention to detail and project management skills.  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to: Excel individually and as a team member.  Travel as needed. Work beyond normal office hours (evenings, nights, and weekends) as needed.  Multitask and work cooperatively with others.  Adapt to a changing library environment.   ·         Licensing/Professional Certifications: Valid driver's license. Physical Requirements: Ability to move medium-weight boxes, books, heavy book truck, or similar items. Other Requirements: Ability to handle material that can contain dust or microscopic mold spores. PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: One or more years of post-MLS experience in research services (research, reference, instruction) in an academic library. Experience developing online learning materials with e-learning technologies/software and other platforms (SpringShare, Adobe Creative Cloud, Camtasia, Articulate, etc.). Experience with instructional and universal design and active learning techniques. Experience with learning management systems (D2L, Blackboard, Canvas, etc.), emerging related technologies (Artificial Intelligence, augmented reality, gamification, etc.), and ADA guidelines.  Experience with instructional planning and design in an academic setting (ACRL Framework for Information Literacy for Higher Education).  Experience in assessing the effectiveness of library services and initiatives. SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: Graduate Assistants and Student Workers.  All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
